      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BLITZBURG (1) can be forgiven for his latest effort at Grafton where he was never able to make an impact over 1600m in a far stronger field. Back in a more suitable assignment and drawn to enjoy a favourable run, he has the ability to bounce back and take this out. MATAWAI (4) has been racing consistently and scored a determined victory at Beaudesert two starts ago before finding the company too rich at Rockhampton 3 weeks ago. Although she rises slightly in the weights, she drops back to a more suitable 1400m, and she is worth another chance. LET'S DO IT AGAIN (8) was below his best at the Sunshine Coast last time but has shown enough ability to warrant respect in this company. Stick with him on a firmer surface. NAILS AND PRIDE (6) bounced straight back into winning form with a strong performance at Gatton last start and another bold showing would not surprise.",
